# DownDraft Engine — API Reference for AI Companions

## Architecture

DownDraft is a TypeScript-first game engine built on Electron + Bun + WebGPU, with an MCP server enabling AI agents to design, build, debug, and manage games via natural language.

**Four execution contexts:**
1. **BrowserWindow** — React UI + input capture (transparent overlay)
2. **Bun main process** — Engine orchestrator, render loop, MCP server, asset manager
3. **Sim worker** — ECS world, game systems, physics, AI, plugins
4. **DB worker** — Persistence layer with schema versioning

## ECS (Entity Component System)

- **Entity**: `{ index: u32, generation: u32 }` — generational indices prevent stale-handle corruption
- **Component**: Plain data class implementing `Component` interface, registered with `ComponentId`
- **Archetype**: Set of component types, SoA column storage for cache-friendly iteration
- **Query**: Declares read/write access to component types, returns matching archetypes
- **System**: Function `(query, resources, commands) => void`
- **Schedule**: Single-threaded by default, dependency-ordered. Multi-threading via plugin/SAB.
- **Events**: Double-buffered channels (written this tick, readable next tick)
- **Commands**: Deferred operations (spawn/despawn, add/remove component) applied at stage boundaries

### Hierarchy
- Parent/child tree stored in side table (not archetype columns) — avoids archetype moves on reparenting
- Dirty-flag propagation: parent Transform change marks children dirty (O(depth))
- Lazy world matrix: computed on read when dirty

### Change Detection
- Per-component `lastChanged` tick counter — O(1) check for consumers
- Cross-thread: `Atomics` on SAB headers for frame sync

## Core API

```typescript
import { World, Camera, MeshBuilder, Component, system, createLogger } from "@downdraft/core";

// Define components
const Health = Component.register<{ current: number; max: number }>("Health", { current: 100, max: 100 });

// Define a system
const damageSystem = system(
  (w: World, dt: number) => {
    const view = w.view([Health]);
    for (const ent of view) {
      const health = w.getComponent(ent, Health);
      if (health && health.data.current <= 0) {
        w.despawn(ent);
      }
    }
  }
);

// Setup
const world = new World();
const camera = new Camera();
camera.setAspect(16, 9);
world.setResource("camera", camera);

// Spawn entities
const entity = world.spawn();
world.addComponent(entity, Health.create({ current: 50, max: 100 }));

// Procedural meshes
const cube = MeshBuilder.cube(1);
const sphere = MeshBuilder.sphere(0.5, 16, 16);
```

## Plugin System

Plugins are loadable packages that register systems, components, resources, and assets.

```typescript
import { Plugin } from "@downdraft/core";

const myPlugin: Plugin = {
  name: "my-plugin",
  install(world: World) {
    // Register components, systems, resources
  },
};

world.registerPlugin(myPlugin);
```

### First-Party Plugins
- `@downdraft/plugin-water` — Gerstner waves, refraction, reflection
- `@downdraft/plugin-physics-rapier` — Rapier physics backend
- `@downdraft/plugin-marching-cubes` — Volumetric deformable terrain
- `@downdraft/plugin-models` — GLTF/GLB/PLY/3DS model loading
- `@downdraft/plugin-devtools` — DevTools panel, scene inspector, GPU debugging
- `@downdraft/plugin-items` — Item definitions and management
- `@downdraft/plugin-inventory` — Inventory system
- `@downdraft/plugin-crafting` — Crafting recipes and system
- `@downdraft/plugin-weather` — Weather simulation
- `@downdraft/plugin-fishing` — Fishing mechanics
- `@downdraft/plugin-economy` — Market/trading system
- `@downdraft/plugin-survival` — Survival stats (hunger, thirst, oxygen)
- `@downdraft/plugin-boats` — Boat building and piloting
- `@downdraft/plugin-wildlife` — Wildlife AI (fish, sharks, eels, etc.)
- `@downdraft/plugin-buoyancy` — Water buoyancy physics
- `@downdraft/plugin-collision` — Entity collision detection
- `@downdraft/plugin-lighting` — Lighting system
- `@downdraft/plugin-networking` — Multiplayer networking

## Builder Modes

| Mode | Use case |
|---|---|
| **dev** | Full DevTools, hot-reload, telemetry. Fastest iteration. |
| **debug** | Local verification on production WebView engine. |
| **prod** | Optimized production build. No devtools/debug overhead. |

## CLI Commands

```
draft new [path] [options]      Scaffold a new game project
draft dev [options]             Start dev server with HMR
draft debug [options]           Run engine in debug mode
draft build [options]           Build for target platform
draft export [options]          Package for distribution
draft assets <cmd>              Manage remote asset packs
```

## MCP Tools (for AI agents)

The MCP server exposes tools for scene management, entity operations, component manipulation, material/shader editing, mesh import, animation, lighting, camera, physics, audio, scripting, asset management, debugging, checkpoints, and build/export.

## Conventions

- **Logging**: No manual `[module]` prefixes — automatic source attribution
- **Loops**: Prefer indexed `for` loops over `for..of`
- **Package manager**: Bun (workspace protocol for internal deps)
